{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/21417-silent-hill","id":21417,"title":"Silent Hill","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-01T20:16:46-08:00","id":21417,"title":"Silent Hill","content":"Como adaptar o cen\u00e1rio de Silent Hill em W:tF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T15:32:41-08:00","id":22644,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Translated:</b></u> How do you adapt the setting of Silent Hill in W:tF?<br /> <br /> You may be interested in picking up the book, Night Horrors Wolfsbane from W:tF. It has a section about a town called Lonesome Forest that you can easily use for a Silent Hill vibe.<br /> Also, Aranis made a <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/Silent_Hill.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Silent Hill pdf. for the New World of Darkness in general.</a><br /> But if you were going the W:tF way, I'll say that there are many ways to make a town like Silent Hill:<br /> It's a Wound, a Idigam has taken over the town, a place where the Hisil has taken over or greatly influenced the town, mass etc.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Translated:</b></u><br /> Usted puede estar interesado en adquirir el libro, Night Horrors Wolfsbane de W: tF. Tiene una secci\u00f3n de un pueblo llamado Solitario bosque que se puede utilizar f\u00e1cilmente para un ambiente Silent Hill.<br /> Aranis hizo un <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/Silent_Hill.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">pdf Silent Hill. para el Nuevo Mundo de las Tinieblas </a><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/Silent_Hill.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">en general</a>.<br /> Pero si se va el W: tF manera, voy a decir que hay muchas maneras de hacer que un pueblo como Silent Hill:<br /> Es una herida, un Idigam ha hecho cargo de la ciudad, un lugar donde el Hisil ha recogido o en gran medida influido en la ciudad, mas etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T01:29:51-08:00","id":23013,"title":"","content":"Try translating it to Portuguese next. He's not speaking in Spanish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T02:29:48-08:00","id":23026,"title":"","content":"Thank Laughing Hyena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T10:04:58-08:00","id":29970,"title":"","content":"Silent Hill is maybe a town on a big wound (like Laughing Hyena said)<br /> The Gauntlet is very thin there.<br /> The whole town moves in and out of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Most of the population is mad or possessed by spirits. They are no longer able to leave their town<br /> Some of the leaders are already claimed.<br /> <br /> Cults of various spirits fight each other.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have to get the trust of the population.<br /> They alos have to close the Wound, fight spirits, fight claimed...<br /> <br /> At the center of the whole a mighty Bale-Hound might rule from behind.<br /> <br /> Silent Hill WTF, fantastic idea, I love it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:28:59-08:00","id":33169,"title":"","content":"I regularly use the siren noise from silent hill to signify the emergence of a wound around the pack even though my game is not silent hill based.<br /> <br /> You can make many of the demons Magath's or you can make them bale hounds under a maijin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","name":"Moxy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1387_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:45:44-08:00","id":62247,"title":"","content":"I just had a thought with this. Why thin the gauntlet when it could just be gone in that section? If you have the town with an incredibly high rat host populace, you wind up with that result. They'd gnaw the gauntlet down to nothing. The building spirits could be some level of corrupt as well, for the wound it'd have to be some town where an incredibly malicious act took place. Like say... a major fire in an orphanage... and a hospital... and a church or 5... an arsonist COULD in theory create that kind of spiritual resonance in the hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}